    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d493-a5">

                <pb facs="0540" n="520" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg520"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Yokohama</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-05-06"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 6, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg to inform you that this morning six
                    or seven Japanese entered my dwelling house and attacked me while dressing. They
                    robbed me of my watch and jewelry about my person, and carried me down into the
                    swamps behind my house, with the intention, as I thought, of killing me, but I
                    was rescued by the presence of Mr. Allmand and Captain Walsh, together with
                    several of the English guards stationed at the new consulate. Thinking myself no
                    longer safe, I have abandoned the house to the Japanese government.</p>
                <p>Yours faithfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S. ROBERTSON.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Geo. S. Fisher</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Consul.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
